  "context": "## The Outlook\nWhat the program forecasts about the near future — anchored on its main prediction: that automation, applied to the systems we actually run, produces more inefficiency and more work before it produces fewer jobs.\n\nDocument Status — Companion Paper (The Outlook) · Series: Informational Friction (a systems theory)\n\nThis paper gathers the forward forecasts of the whole program — across all four series: The Cost of Clarity (information theory), The Attribution Gap (economics), Human Intelligence Debt (organizational theory), and the systems-theory series (Papers 1–3). Each forecast is conditional: it holds only while the falsification test it rests on survives. Those tests are stated in full in the companion refutation paper; here each forecast names the test it depends on so an examiner can follow the thread.\nEtiquetas: Capacidad humana y deuda de inteligencia 45.46%; Cartografía y señales de ecosistema 9.09%; Economía, costes y liquidez 45.45%\nFicha: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/the-outlook-t1494/\nDocumento de origen: https://tegrity.ai/the-outlook/\n\n",
